    "title": "Fever's Season Ends in Loss to Las Vegas Aces",
    "text": "• Caitlin Clark and the Indiana Fever lost to the Las Vegas Aces 94-83 in Game 3.\n• A'ja Wilson led the Aces with 36 points, including 21 by halftime.\n• Clark finished with 18 points on 6-of-18 shooting.\n• The Fever kept the game within single digits until the final two minutes.\n• Clark took a sharp elbow to the face from Jewell Loyd in the fourth quarter.\n• Clark's mouth was bleeding profusely after the incident.\n• Clark ran back onto the court to continue playing despite her injury.\n• A'ja Wilson was not ejected for a technical foul in Game 2 despite confronting a fan in the stands.\n• A'ces coach Becky Hammon defended Wilson, saying she was pushed and shoved by the fan.\n• Fever head coach Stephanie White was criticized for not defending her players against dirty play.\n• The Fever finished the season 28-16 as the sixth seed.\n• Caitlin Clark averaged 20.0 points, 9.7 assists, and 4.0 rebounds per game in the series.\n• Clark averaged 22.3 points, 8.3 assists, and 4.0 rebounds per game in the regular season.\n• Clark has not won a playoff series in her career.",
    "summary": "The season came to an end for Clark and the Indiana Fever with a 94-83 loss to A'ja Wilson and the reigning champion Las Vegas Aces in Thursday's decisive Game 3. A'ja Wilson's technical foul in Game 2 was the talk of the town, largely overshadowing Caitlin Clark's historic postseason milestones. While opponents treated Caitlin Clark and Sophie Cunningham like punching bags, White hid behind spineless PR fluff instead of defending her stars.",
